                <pb facs="0272" n="230" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg230"/>

                <head>The seizure of the Magicienne.</head>
                <p>Mr. Samuel Baker, of Liverpool, the owner of the Magicienne, has received the
                    following despatch from the foreign office:</p>
                <p rendition="#right">
                    <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">April</hi> 3.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: I am directed by Earl Russell to
                    acquaint you, in reply to your letter of the 23d ult., that her Majesty’s
                    minister at Washington will be instructed to apply to the government of the
                    United States for full compensation to the parties interested in the
                    Magicienne.</p>
                <p>I am, gentlemen, your obedient servant,</p>
                <p rendition="#right">E. HAMMOND.</p>
                <p>Messrs. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Baker.</hi></p>
                <p>This vessel was seized on her voyage to Matamoras by a federal cruiser, and was
                    sent to Key West, where she was released.</p>
            </div>
